-- Ishigaki guide — data backup
--
-- The live contents of the guide, exported from Supabase on 2026-09-13.
-- This replaces the placeholder starter set that used to live in
-- 03_seed.sql: that was 39 invented entries, this is the real guide.
--
-- Run AFTER 01_schema.sql, 02_rls.sql and 04_photos.sql, since the photo
-- rows need both tables to exist. Safe to re-run: ids are preserved and
-- every insert is "on conflict do nothing", so it restores what is missing
-- and leaves what is there alone.
--
-- Ids matter. place_photos.place_id is a foreign key, so an import that
-- generated fresh uuids would orphan every photo.
--
-- NOT covered: the image files themselves. Those are binaries in the
-- place-photos storage bucket, and restoring this file alone would give you
-- working text with broken pictures. Download the bucket separately.

insert into places (
  id, name, name_ja, category, area, blurb, notes,
  lat, lng, must_do, booking, best_time, website
) values
('4c5ee9b8-b029-468b-840a-70fe3dfdecf0','ANA InterContinental Ishigaki Resort','ANAインターコンチネンタル石垣リゾート','practical','Ishigaki City','Chez vous','Fronts Maezato Beach, the nearest swimming beach to the city.','24.3352036727934','124.187644935582','f',NULL,NULL,'https://www.anaintercontinental-ishigaki.jp/'),
('f3d4c9d0-84f6-4f69-be9f-96c70996bf51','Banna Park — North Gate','バンナ公園 北口','sights','Central','The nature entrance to Banna Park: the wild plant garden, the egg-shaped migratory bird observatory and the easiest walking are all clustered here. Free parking.','This is the gate to use for nature spotting rather than views. From spring into early summer the firefly road here fills with Yaeyama fireflies at dusk — they are tiny, they only perform for half an hour or so after sunset, and the park shuts at 21:00, so time it carefully.','24.3849968947755','124.174790693255','f',NULL,'Dusk in spring for the fireflies; early morning for birds','https://banna.jp/map'),
('f6c2db65-464c-457e-9b14-1e7ac1e28b6d','Banna Park — South Gate','バンナ公園 南口','sights','Central','The entrance closest to town, and the start of the Banna Skyline road that runs up over the ridge to the north gate past three lookouts.','Use this one if you are driving the skyline rather than walking the forest. Free parking, ten minutes from the centre of Ishigaki.','24.3689262536758','124.158187819447','f',NULL,NULL,'https://banna.jp/map'),
('08919780-14c7-4c6c-9468-d8ee2d5c5393','Banna Park — West Gate','バンナ公園 西口','sights','Central','The quietest of the three main entrances, on the western side of the park.','Worth knowing about mainly because the park is enormous — over five zones — and picking the right gate saves a long walk or a long drive round.','24.3744489100221','124.155618293255','f',NULL,NULL,'https://banna.jp/map'),
('c6f9e3ac-7b51-41db-b3ba-51ea84493666','Bar Blue Cafe','BAR BLUE CAFE','drink','Ishigaki City','A cocktail bar in Misaki-cho with a DJ booth by the door — roomy and unhurried, which is not the norm in that warren of tiny places.','Opens late, around 20:30, and runs to roughly 01:00. Do not confuse it with the daytime Blue Cafe in the hostel by the ferry terminal: same name, different street, and it shuts in the afternoon. Instagram @bar__blue_cafe.','24.3378','124.156','f',NULL,'Late — from about 20:30','https://www.instagram.com/bar__blue_cafe/'),
('a9adf5ce-3ac5-41b8-aaf9-d827799c9db7','Bar Cocosone','BAR COCOSONE','drink','Ishigaki City','The most fun bar in Okinawa: we are old friends of Chibi the owner.','Cash only. Put the cash in the bowl on the bar when you order. Looks completely shut from the street but just go in. Apparently has been written up in guides, so there are quite a few foreigners now, but a lot of locals too. His awamori cocktails are pretty good!','24.3410194158289','124.157446006745','t',NULL,'From 19:00; closing days are irregular',NULL),
('34530530-a6f8-462d-8cca-18f2677ead6e','Blue Coral','ブルーコーラル','daytrip','East coast','Small-boat snorkel trips out to the blue coral at Shiraho, the largest colony in the northern hemisphere. Nine minutes from the airport, and no scuba licence needed.','Worth knowing before you get in: the blue coral is not blue on the outside. The surface is beige and brown, and the blue is underneath. Knowing that in advance makes it more remarkable, not less. Well run, friendly, and they take you to spots you would never find on your own. Instagram @bluecoraldiveshop.','24.3553682936318','124.244602093255','t','Book ahead — 0980-86-7799','Tours at 08:30 and 13:30','http://bluecoral73.okinawa/'),
('35b365d2-8de7-4828-8ec0-21950978f5b1','Doug''s Burger','ダグズ・バーガー 石垣島店','food','Ishigaki City','Surprisingly nice burgers! Not Ishigki beef, but from a nearby island.','On the Ginza-dori side of the arcade, open every day, roughly 11:00 to 20:00 with the dining room closing a little earlier.','24.34','124.1558','f',NULL,'Lunch','https://www.dougsburger.com/'),
('4b65e5c5-a294-4304-b79f-daa3da04fc45','Ishigaki Port Ferry Terminal','石垣港離島ターミナル','practical','Ishigaki City','Every ferry to every other Yaeyama island leaves from here: Taketomi, Iriomote, Kohama, Hateruma.','Two operators run near-identical schedules and you buy on the day at the counter. Hateruma boats cancel often in wind.','24.3364','124.1553','f',NULL,NULL,NULL),
('17f3bb07-1a8d-4cb5-b4e9-efc3e7990857','Ishigaki Public Market','石垣市公設市場','shop','Ishigaki City','Two floors of island produce, fish, chilli oil, sea salt and Ishigaki beef, with craft stalls upstairs.','Good for snacks, and for working out what is in season before you order it in a restaurant.','24.3401','124.1554','f',NULL,'Mornings',NULL),
('facbdfd0-8e6c-4283-8b68-3bbe34663c72','Ishigaki-yaki Pottery Studio','石垣焼窯元','shop','West coast','The studio of Haruhiko Kaneko - I have introduced you I hope','On the Nagura Bay road,  south of Kabira. Haruhiko fuses glass into ceramic to get a blue the colour of the reef outside his window. Work of his are in the British Museum and the Musée Guimet. I''ve met him and his wife a few times in Paris and Ishigaki.','24.4161040794494','124.134397164418','t',NULL,NULL,'https://www.ishigaki-yaki.com/en/'),
('96c753ff-03ad-4a0b-b62f-ea8fc442142e','JA Yuratiku Market','ゆらてぃく市場','shop','Ishigaki City','The biggest farmers market on the island and the southernmost farm shop in Japan — fruit, vegetables, meat and Ishigaki beef straight off local farms, well under supermarket prices.','Go at about 10:00. At nine it is half empty, because the farmers drop stock off through the morning, and by evening the best of it has gone. It also sells raw Ishigaki beef to cook yourself if you have a kitchen. Closed the first three days of January, the last day of Obon, and roughly one day a month.','24.3420140386655','124.154003049073','t',NULL,'Around 10:00 — not at opening, not in the evening','https://www.ja-okinawa.or.jp/farmersmarket/detail.php?id=542'),
('03314099-69f3-456a-bb48-373b5914e5cc','Kabira Bay','川平湾','shop','Kabira','Very nice beach walk and pearl shop','No swimming.','24.4612323935656','124.14349724905','f',NULL,'Late morning, once the sun is high enough to light the sand',NULL),
('cb1bdf9d-fe1f-44a3-a1b0-caa3d6b1d0a3','Manta Scramble','マンタスクランブル','daytrip','Kabira','A cleaning station off Kabira Ishizaki where reef mantas queue up over the coral heads.','Boat access only, from Kabira. Dive and snorkel operators both run trips, and it is the single best thing in the water here.','24.4872169499206','124.118441135582','f','Book ahead in summer — boats fill up','June to November, best odds in autumn',NULL),
('d05d3094-5b38-4cc7-8ce5-32f64d520628','New Ishigaki Airport','南ぬ島石垣空港','practical','East coast','The island airport, about thirty minutes east of town, with direct flights from Naha, Tokyo and Osaka.','Pick the rental car up here rather than in town. The airport bus into the city takes about forty minutes.','24.3964','124.245','f',NULL,NULL,NULL),
('0c0103d0-cf7b-4d92-9764-dd6842a02530','Phantom Island sandbar','幻の島(浜島)','daytrip','Off-island','A crescent of bare white sand that surfaces out of open sea at low tide and then disappears again.','Boat trips run from Ishigaki port, usually combined with snorkelling off Kohama.','24.321','124.018','f','Tour only, and tide-dependent','Low tide',NULL),
('9ddbff51-16f6-490b-b10e-b712df8e9c04','Shiraho Sunday Market','白保日曜市','shop','East coast','A small weekly market in the old coral centre at Shiraho, run by people from the village selling island vegetables, fruit and whatever else they have that morning.','Local small market, mainly cash only. Go without big expectations and it is lovely. Check @shirahonichiyoichi before setting out, because they skip some Sundays. Some vendors cash only.','24.3521089034826','124.24308526184','t',NULL,'Sundays only, 10:00 to 13:00','https://www.instagram.com/shirahonichiyoichi/'),
('4a974c12-cd62-4b9d-a065-2f9ef70de951','Taketomi Island','竹富島','daytrip','Off-island','Fifteen minutes by ferry: one village of red-tiled roofs, coral walls and white sand lanes, with water buffalo carts and no traffic.','Touristy but very unique and fun and a lot to see. Worth a day. We saw a habu snake here, but apparently that is very rare.','24.3313','124.087','f',NULL,'First ferry, or late afternoon',NULL),
('d3ca6d64-5cff-410d-90ad-74eccf395545','Torinji Temple','桃林寺','sights','Ishigaki City','Founded in 1614, the oldest temple in the Yaeyamas, with a pair of weathered wooden guardian kings in the gate.','Ten minutes on foot from the port. Quiet and small — worth twenty minutes.','24.3439344860813','124.155676406745','f',NULL,NULL,NULL),
('6afcc8e1-d6b0-4e96-bd70-14af59bb125e','Yakiniku MARU','石垣牛 MARU','food','Ishigaki City','Our favorite Ishigaki beef yakiniku','Dinner only, from 17:00. Popular with locals. Either book in advance or queue up outside before they open at 17:00. If ooing as the entire group will need reservations.','24.3396','124.16','t','Book ahead — it fills up','Dinner','https://ishigaki-maru.com/'),
('96a43edd-9050-4e2b-8a64-3f0281993094','Yonehara Beach','米原ビーチ','sights','Yonehara','Apparently the best shore snorkelling on the island — living coral and fish start a few metres off the sand. We did not snorkel there, but here for the record.','Take this seriously: there is a strong current past the reef edge and no lifeguard. Stay inside the reef, wear a rash guard against the sun, and watch for stonefish — reef shoes help.','24.4540627415001','124.185677873018','f',NULL,'High tide on a calm morning',NULL)
on conflict (id) do nothing;

